Shipping family: partitions of a 240-vertex, degree-5 graph into six E-sets of 40 vertices. It derives from the paper’s E-set definition and avoids its explicitly solvable transposition graphs. Hardness is supported by the fixed-target \(K_q\)-Cover NP-completeness result for \(q\ge4\) ([paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2007.09736), [complexity source](https://www.cs.uoregon.edu/Reports/TR-1994-018.pdf)).

Key results:

- All G1–G8 gates pass.
- Random guessing: 0/200,000 balanced candidates.
- Adversaries: 0/8 for outlier, greedy, and 128-restart attacks.
- Canonical key: 60/60 invariance checks; 20/20 unrelated keys distinct.
- Oracle verdict: `hardened` at `medium`, `{"n": 40, "q": 6}`.
- Three distinct final oracle models failed; all replies parsed correctly.

An earlier 100-vertex preset held against the oracle panel but was rejected because random restarts solved 7/8 seeds. That failure and the remaining caveats are documented in the README.
